WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.568
As you know, the U.S.

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:01.968
right now

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.303
could be just three weeks away

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.372
from defaulting on its debt.

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:06.639
That could mean millions of jobs

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:07.273
lost, people

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:08.041
not getting

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:09.409
their Social Security payments.

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:10.610
People believe it would put the U.S.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.679
economy into a recession.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:13.446
On that topic,

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.148
I want to bring in Marta Sevilla,

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.816
a student here at Saint Anselm.

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:17.984
She is an undeclared voter

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:19.486
who did not vote in 2020.

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:20.854
Marta, what's your question?

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:22.322
Hi, Mr. President.

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:23.189
So my question

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.224
is, what do you think

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:25.425
about the United States

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:27.060
current debt situation

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.462
and how can we move forward?

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.131
Such an important question.

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:33.900
So we're at $33 trillion in number

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.302
that nobody ever thought possible

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.771
when we had our economy

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:38.705
rocking and rolling

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.306
just prior to COVID coming in.

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.641
Like literally

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:44.310
we were making a fortune and oil.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:44.811
We were going to make

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:46.012
so much money from oil,

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:47.881
we're going to start paying off debt.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.182
But then with COVID coming

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:50.216
and we had to do other things,

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:51.885
we had to keep this country alive

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.553
because it was so serious.

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.088
But we have to get the country back.

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:56.623
We have to lower energy prices.

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:57.991
We have to lower interest rates.

00:00:57.991 --> 00:00:59.793
Interest rates are through the roof.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:00.860
Energy has to come down.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.028
It all has to come down

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.997
and we have to start paying off debt.

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:07.033
But when we have a debt limit

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.535
and they use that very seriously,

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:09.602
I mean, they came in Schumer

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:11.571
came in with Nancy Pelosi

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.540
and they were using and will violate

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.541
it, will do whatever.

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:15.942
They talked a whole lot different

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:16.876
than they do right now.

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:18.445
I say to the Republicans out there,

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:19.913
Congressman, senators,

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:22.449
if they don't give you massive cuts,

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:24.684
you're going to have to do a default.

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:25.618
And I don't believe

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:27.487
they're going to do a default

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:28.855
because I think the Democrats

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.723
will absolutely cave

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:31.491
because you don't

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:32.892
want to have that happen.

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:34.194
But it's better than what

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:35.595
we're doing right now

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:36.896
because we're spending money

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.298
like drunken sailors.

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:39.399
So just to be clear, Mr.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:39.766
President,

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.768
you think the US should default

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:43.203
if the White House does not agree

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:44.671
to the spending cuts, Republicans

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:45.572
might as well do it now

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.040
because you'll do it later.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.741
Because we have to save this country.

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:50.410
Our country is dying.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:51.978
Our country is being destroyed

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:54.147
by stupid people, by very stupid people.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.216
You once said that using that

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:57.484
that using the debt

00:01:57.484 --> 00:01:59.452
ceiling is a negotiating wedge.

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:00.520
Just could not happen.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.222
You you said that when you were

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:03.123
president.

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:03.957
So why is it different

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:05.358
now that you're out of office now?

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:13.933
I'm not president.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.803
The US defaulting would be massively.

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:17.670
Well, you don't know

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:18.805
every one of the problems.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:19.506
You don't know.

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:20.673
It's psychological.

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:21.808
It's really psychological

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:22.842
more than anything else.

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:24.144
And it could be very bad.

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:25.245
It could be maybe nothing.

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:25.879
Maybe it's a

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:28.314
you have a bad week or a bad day.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:31.050
But look, you have to cut your costs.

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:34.487
We're we're spending $7 trillion on

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:37.023
much of it on nonsense.

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:40.160
$7 trillion on nonsense.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.327
We've got to have actually said

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:42.896
voter to get all of that money

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:43.763
that was wasted.

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:44.297
And frankly,

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:46.132
the Senate should have never approved it.

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:47.934
Get all that money that was wasted.

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.035
And if they don't get rid of that,

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:50.637
you'll have to default.

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:50.837
Mr.

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.238
President, we've got another voter here.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:52.705
And by the way,

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:52.906
you're going

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:54.474
to default eventually anyway,

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:56.309
but it's going to be much messier.

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:57.777
I don't think you'll have to default.

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:59.746
I think if the Republicans hold strong

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:02.081
and they say we want five,

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:04.717
let's say we want $5 trillion off,

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:06.519
I really think the Democrats have

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:08.188
no choice but to do it.

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:09.189
And if I win,

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:09.889
they're going to be doing

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:10.990
the same thing to me in two

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.292
years, I guarantee you that.

